# Test Example (TypeScript with HTTP mocking)

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from 'vitest';

describe('post_activity_result', () => {
  it('should successfully post activity result', async () => {
    // Mock HTTP POST request
    const mockFetch = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({
      status: 201,
      json: async () => ({ execution_id: 'exec_123' })
    });
    global.fetch = mockFetch;

    // Call tool
    const result = await postActivityResult({
      activityId: 'act_123',
      result: { success: true, duration: 5000, cost: 0.05, tokens: { input: 100, output: 200, cache: 0 } }
    });

    expect(result.status).toBe('success');
    expect(mockFetch).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
      expect.stringContaining('/api/v1/learning-loop/executions'),
      expect.objectContaining({ method: 'POST' })
    );
  });

  it('should handle timeout gracefully', async () => {
    // Mock timeout
    const mockFetch = vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error('Timeout'));
    global.fetch = mockFetch;

    const result = await postActivityResult({
      activityId: 'act_123',
      result: { success: true, duration: 5000, cost: 0.05, tokens: { input: 100, output: 200, cache: 0 } }
    });

    expect(result.status).toBe('error');
    expect(result.learning_enabled).toBe(false);
  });
});
```

# Success Criteria

- ✓ Tests pass without errors
- ✓ Tests mock HTTP requests (not in-memory operations)
- ✓ Tests cover success case (201 response)
- ✓ Tests cover error cases (timeout, HTTP errors)
- ✓ Test output shows all assertions passing

